Patch 0014-moe-batched-load.patch for vLLM, base commit 77154ca6116ae34cbfe314beef1016bde9b63989 (vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-77154ca6116ae34cbfe314beef1016bde9b63989).
What: Reads the routed experts' weights from the checkpoint in large parallel preadv calls into fresh tensors, in the same order and with the same bytes, instead of copying each expert out of the memory map a page at a time; a cold boot's weight load drops from about 450-540 s to about 120 s with identical served text (QWEN38_BATCHED_LOAD=0 turns it off). The design follows TensorFold's loader (merged large reads).
Upstream: no vLLM PR. written for this recipe.
This file modifies vLLM (Apache-2.0); the vLLM copyright and SPDX lines in the files it changes are kept.

